[[17592186059578 :question/problem "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}5 & -4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"] [17592186059578 :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and $y,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}5x-4y=-12 \\\\ 3x+y=1.\\end{cases}\n$$"] [17592186059579 :question/problem "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}\\frac{c}{2}=a \\\\ 5+3b-a=4c \\\\ d=1\\end{cases}\n$$"] [17592186059579 :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $a,b,c,d$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}-a+0b+\\frac{1}{2}c+0d=0 \\\\ -a+3b-4c+0d=-5 \\\\ 0a+0b+0c+d=1\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$"]]